@meeting captainAllClear.rough
// EW1 (events writer), the storm update: the all-clear, Sunday Day 14 at 10:00, the observation room, when the storm
// went roughly (one file per band: captainAllClear.smooth, .bumpy, .rough; replaces MEETING_SCRIPTS.captainAllClear).
// Four of the five are called in on their day off (the Captain, Calder, Sato, Holt; Vance is on duty), and they say
// so (the user's answer). FOR EV1: after Calder's "Mine too" line the game inserts the Captain's line to you from
// the bank keys event.ionStorm.allclear.you.commended | .jobs | .none (content/banks/event-ionStorm.lines), as the
// game's script does today with c.mine.jobs: the commendation letter comes now (the user's answer 8).
title: The all-clear
from: Commander Teo Vance
gist: Notes from the observation room: the storm passed at 09:40, long blackouts, a scorched relay room and food binned. Comms are back; expect a queue at the booths. Party in the bow lounge at 19:00.
== lines
vance: The Captain. Who is, for the record, off duty today.   [nod]
marrow: So is most of this room. Thank you for coming in. Dr. Sato?   [gesture]
sato: The front passed us at 09:40. Readings are back to background. It's over.
sato: I'd have come in anyway. You don't sleep through the end of a storm.
marrow: Then let's say so. That was a hard one, and the ship shows it.   [nod]
calder: The relay room's a mess. We'll be patching for a week.
holt: Watch reports no injuries. Some short tempers. Mine included. It's my day off.   [sigh]
calder: Mine too. Nobody tell my rota.   [laugh]
? choice
* It was good to be useful.   rel:marrow+1,calder+1
  marrow: It always is. Remember that on the dull days.   [nod]
* Is there a party?   rel:vance+1
  vance: Bow lounge, 19:00. The Captain insists.   [gesture]
* (Just nod)
  marrow: Good.   [nod]
marrow: Right. I'll tell the ship. Then I'm going back to my Sunday.   [laugh]
